         spatialAssetURI:
           type: string
+          description: >-
+            The address of this node's content: a model, or the Spatial, Node or wow/world resource of
+            any world, which is then shown at this node. A client tells them apart by the media type of
+            the answer, never by the address or the content: application/wow+json marks a Web of Worlds
+            resource. The including node stands in for the included node's parent. A whole world shows
+            its default graph, and its other anchored graphs where their GeoPoses put them. The included
+            world's environment does not apply to the host. The host sets a nesting limit and a budget of
+            included graphs, which it hands out in tree order (depth first, children in order); it
+            detects cycles by URL and shows a placeholder on failure.
